{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"USN-8930-1","published":"2026-10-14T16:23:58Z","modified":"2026-10-17T13:11:53.933670443Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74220","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74221","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74222","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74225"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-74220","CVE-2026-74221","CVE-2026-74222","CVE-2026-74225","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74220","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74221","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74222","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-74225"],"summary":"u-boot vulnerabilities","details":"Shahriyar Jalayeri and Mehrun P. Hunter discovered that U-Boot\nincorrectly handled certain NFS READ and NFS READLINK responses. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to trigger a buffer overflow,\nresulting in a denial of service or arbitrary code execution.\n(CVE-2026-74220, CVE-2026-74221)\n\nShahriyar Jalayeri and Mehrun P. Hunter discovered that U-Boot\nincorrectly handled certain HTTP data storage failures in its lwIP\nimplementation. An attacker could possibly use this issue to trigger a\nuse-after-free, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-74222)\n\nShahriyar Jalayeri and Mehrun P. Hunter discovered that U-Boot did not\nproperly validate certain DHCPv6 option lengths during network boot. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to trigger out-of-bounds memory\naccess, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-74225)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"u-boot","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/u-boot?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2016.01+dfsg1-2ubuntu5+esm2"}]}],"versions":["2015.04+dfsg1-2ubuntu1","2015.10+dfsg1-2","2015.10+dfsg1-3","2015.10+dfsg1-4","2016.01+dfsg1-1","2016.01+dfsg1-1ubuntu1","2016.01+dfsg1-2ubuntu1","2016.01+dfsg1-2ubuntu2","2016.01+dfsg1-2ubuntu3","2016.01+dfsg1-2ubuntu5","2016.01+dfsg1-2ubuntu5+esm1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Availa